-- title:
--   Pure braids are products of half-twists
-- statement:
--   Every pure braid is a product of elementary half-twists: the image of the pure braid group $P_n$ in the geometric braid group, under the map induced by the projection from ordered to unordered configurations, is contained in the subgroup generated by the classes $[\mathrm{ht}_1], \ldots, [\mathrm{ht}_{n-1}]$.
--
--   This is the substantive half of Teorema 3.11. Generation of the full braid group splits into two parts along the exact sequence $1 	o P_n 	o B_n 	o \mathfrak{S}_n 	o 1$. The quotient part is easy, since the half-twists map onto the adjacent transpositions and those generate the symmetric group; given that, an arbitrary braid can be corrected by a product of half-twists until it becomes pure, and what remains is to know that pure braids are already products of half-twists. That is the statement here.
--
--   Classically it is proved by the Fadell–Neuwirth induction. Forgetting the last point gives a fibration of the ordered configuration space over the ordered configuration space on one fewer point, with fibre a punctured plane; the resulting short exact sequence
--
--   $$1 	o F_{n-1} 	o P_n 	o P_{n-1} 	o 1$$
--
--   splits, so $P_n$ is generated by $P_{n-1}$ together with the free factor. The free factor is generated by the loops $A_{i n}$ in which the last strand encircles one earlier strand, and each $A_{in}$ is an explicit word in half-twists --- conjugating $\mathrm{ht}_{n-1}^2$ by a product of half-twists that carries strand $i$ into position. Induction on $n$ finishes.
--
--   Stated as a containment rather than an equality because the reverse inclusion is false in general: the half-twists themselves are not pure.
-- source:
--   Tarcha, Braid Theory and the Artin Presentation, Teorema 3.11; Birman, Braids, Links and Mapping Class Groups, Chapter 1, Proposition 1.1 and Theorem 1.4.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BraidsLinksMCG_ConfigSpace
import Definitions.Def_TarchaBraids_HalfTwist

namespace TarchaBraids

open BraidsLinksMCG

theorem pureBraid_le_halfTwist_closure (n : ℕ) :
    (FundamentalGroup.map (configProj n) (baseOrdered n)).range ≤
      Subgroup.closure (Set.range (fun i : Fin (n - 1) => halfTwistBraid n i)) := by sorry

end TarchaBraids
